<title>TURKEY: Turkish Cimentas H1 profits plummet.</title>
<headline>Turkish Cimentas H1 profits plummet.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     7.19  vs     969.45</p>
<p>    Net profit			5.03  vs     678.61</p>
<p>    Net sales		   6,007.44  vs   2,596.57</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  1,590.74  vs     675.92</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  202.06  vs     202.25</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     1,755.20  vs	95.84</p>
<p>    Total debts		 8,423.63  vs   3,585.71</p>
<p>    Equity			5,005.06  vs   3,530.53</p>
<p>    Capital			 700.00  vs     700.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Shares of Turkish cement and breeze block producer Cimentas Izmir Cimento Fabrikasi Turk AS are also listed on the Munich bourse.</p>
<p>The company, which bought small-scale state-owned cement factory Kars Cimento from the privatisation administration for $22.5 million in late 1996, has several ongoing investments.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
